{"content":[{"c":["EDH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Hebrew name of an altar built in God’s honor by the Reubenites, Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.22.10,34","r":"Josh.22.10,34","rawR":"Josh.22.10,34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.22.10,34","value":"Josh.22.10,34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 22:10, 34"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg) when these tribes took possession of Gilead. The name means “witness.” The Hebrew Masoretic Text and the Greek Septuagint do not contain the word, but it has the authority of a few ancient manuscripts."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Edh","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 22:10, 34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.22.10,34","rawQueryValue":"Josh.22.10,34","sourceRefExact":"Josh.22.10,34"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"62a4ba97a218170dc505a8121a437e27ef33e1408fde0ed5f36f0281a6156489","sourceItemName":"Edh","sourceItemOrder":32,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Edh","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Edh*","title":"Edh*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}